                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "da32b06a-d308-4769-a390-379e36e57faa",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f970464-eddd-3265-a15e-dea920295695",
                        "source_sense_id": "11c92fde-6fae-3d03-938e-6faebe239496",
                        "target_lang_word": "unguardedly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unguardedly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "094b584f-a295-301f-9f6e-589032ca9d27",
                                        "entry_id": "3581c337-ce5e-3a92-b3f6-4b58a98c289a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an unguarded manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d64c963f-c6f7-4807-9ac8-a6f25ea67f40",
                                                "sense_id": "094b584f-a295-301f-9f6e-589032ca9d27",
                                                "text": "As for great wigs, upon which I may be thought to have spoken my mind too freely—I beg leave to qualify whatever has been unguardedly said to their dispraise or prejudice, by one general declaration—That I have no abhorrence whatever, nor do I detest and abjure either great wigs or long beards […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a21c060d-82f1-4168-8ee8-802e687486ae",
                                                "sense_id": "094b584f-a295-301f-9f6e-589032ca9d27",
                                                "text": "Alas! in those acute moments, Milford snatched to his lip the poisonous cup of intoxication, and during that delirium, if her hapless form met his glaring eye, the hand of passion would unguardedly wreak its vengeance on the insensate object of his wrath, and thus execrating Hymen, and all his votaries, this sullen captive would, till the exhausted storm of passion sunk him in agitated slumbers, while his sleepy wife was dreaming by his side, of all the glorious pomps and vanities to which her husband’s consequence, and her own imagined charms had raised her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "970ced14-7a2a-48c0-bc69-d28f410b9a3f",
                                                "sense_id": "094b584f-a295-301f-9f6e-589032ca9d27",
                                                "text": "And Fanny, though I hope I do justice to my sisters['] good qualities, I think it very possible that they might, one or both, be more desirous of being admired by Crawford, and might shew that desire rather more unguardedly than was perfectly prudent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e416ca74-5be7-4258-9648-5bd53a60b3a4",
                                                "sense_id": "094b584f-a295-301f-9f6e-589032ca9d27",
                                                "text": "But Jane and Jacob are going to have quantities of champagne. Not tipsy, you understand, but at their best, and unguardedly appreciative of each other and us."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9bc2b21d-3052-48e5-9fb0-2a5ce81c6d6c",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f970464-eddd-3265-a15e-dea920295695",
                        "source_sense_id": "11c92fde-6fae-3d03-938e-6faebe239496",
                        "target_lang_word": "head first",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "head first",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88b6d313-80c8-3003-a12e-b4a54af6c84f",
                                        "entry_id": "ab2dde2b-12c3-3d68-8854-518ffcd5c7f2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With the head first or foremost."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b940598-b341-4ebb-976a-8768fbb43843",
                                                "sense_id": "88b6d313-80c8-3003-a12e-b4a54af6c84f",
                                                "text": "I shot head first off of the bank like a frog, clothes and all on, and struck out for the canoe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52e9030c-76e9-44e6-aae0-ec5b3bffe1e7",
                                                "sense_id": "88b6d313-80c8-3003-a12e-b4a54af6c84f",
                                                "text": "He must be able to spring from the floor to about twice his own height, gradually turning over as he rises, so as to come down again head first."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ddb1228-fa61-4bac-b8aa-909cd98a023d",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f970464-eddd-3265-a15e-dea920295695",
                        "source_sense_id": "11c92fde-6fae-3d03-938e-6faebe239496",
                        "target_lang_word": "headforemost",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "headforemost",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49039769-fb6a-3197-abf5-4b32ab356fc1",
                                        "entry_id": "0416c777-aeb5-317f-b034-8b3c672f4ef6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "headfirst"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57a813db-bf5d-4b2a-bf61-e8d68f5f0669",
                                                "sense_id": "49039769-fb6a-3197-abf5-4b32ab356fc1",
                                                "text": "’Twere best at once to sink to peace,\n⁠Like birds the charming serpent draws,\n⁠To drop head-foremost in the jaws\nOf vacant darkness and to cease."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cb423b5-eb53-4291-a6f4-0d80e9456d9a",
                                                "sense_id": "49039769-fb6a-3197-abf5-4b32ab356fc1",
                                                "text": "Exerting all his remaining strength he rushed down the bank, dropped his rifle, and plunged headforemost into the stream."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d88fab6e-ed81-4681-97b4-cd816380601d",
                                                "sense_id": "49039769-fb6a-3197-abf5-4b32ab356fc1",
                                                "text": "He doubled up and went headforemost to the ground."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7bc98fb-69bc-4c59-82fc-2548a24fc118",
                                                "sense_id": "49039769-fb6a-3197-abf5-4b32ab356fc1",
                                                "text": "Quick, or I'll land you headforemost in that pond, you infernal old hag!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2654b9c7-ec7f-4fc5-a089-7c321d0dec78",
                                                "sense_id": "49039769-fb6a-3197-abf5-4b32ab356fc1",
                                                "text": "Just then there came a loud crash and an ominous rumbling and pounding from the heart of the ship—her machinery had broken loose, and was dashing its way toward the bow, tearing out partitions and bulkheads as it went—the stern rose rapidly high above them; for a moment she seemed to pause there—a vertical shaft protruding from the bosom of the ocean, and then swiftly she dove headforemost beneath the waves."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c81c15d6-fa38-4915-8575-f11181c71b55",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f970464-eddd-3265-a15e-dea920295695",
                        "source_sense_id": "11c92fde-6fae-3d03-938e-6faebe239496",
                        "target_lang_word": "thoughtlessly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thoughtlessly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5aaac76-934d-3735-8545-bfde7458d420",
                                        "entry_id": "2e30de60-8757-3e90-96dc-e0f3fea755fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Done without thinking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51e9fcfb-479a-4bc8-8229-55e92b1ddfad",
                                                "sense_id": "a5aaac76-934d-3735-8545-bfde7458d420",
                                                "text": "He thoughtlessly invited her to come jogging, as he knew she hated exercise."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cf613fd-812b-45bd-bb9b-ba7290e59b16",
                                                "sense_id": "a5aaac76-934d-3735-8545-bfde7458d420",
                                                "text": "The railway ran through the resort's narrow streets up to Weymouth Quay station, with thoughtlessly parked vehicles sometimes having to be bumped out of the way."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
